\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Three different methods for representing traces (embedding the raw trace, embedding a structured summary based on a generic rubric, and embedding a structured summary based on a task-specific rubric) evaluated on preserving / removing properties (i)--(v). The representation based on \textsc  {trubric}{} is better at preserving relevant signal ((i) Task and (ii) Correctness) while mitigating information about system idiosyncrasies ((iii) System Identity, (iv) Model Family, and (v) Harness).}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:radar}{{1}{3}{Three different methods for representing traces (embedding the raw trace, embedding a structured summary based on a generic rubric, and embedding a structured summary based on a task-specific rubric) evaluated on preserving / removing properties (i)--(v). The representation based on \trubric {} is better at preserving relevant signal ((i) Task and (ii) Correctness) while mitigating information about system idiosyncrasies ((iii) System Identity, (iv) Model Family, and (v) Harness)}{figure.1}{}}
