\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The 2-d Product Kernel Perspective Space (PKPS) induced with raw trace embeddings (top) and the \textsc  {trubric}{} embeddings (bottom) under different number of reference systems and number of task executions. Each dot is a system colored by full benchmark score on SWE-bench Verified. The manifold of systems under the \textsc  {trubric}{} embeddings is more strongly correlated with the full benchmark score in paired settings. We report the average Mean Absolute Error (MAE) under leave-one-system-out (LOSO) protocol to quantify this observation.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pkps}{{2}{5}{The 2-d Product Kernel Perspective Space (PKPS) induced with raw trace embeddings (top) and the \trubric {} embeddings (bottom) under different number of reference systems and number of task executions. Each dot is a system colored by full benchmark score on SWE-bench Verified. The manifold of systems under the \trubric {} embeddings is more strongly correlated with the full benchmark score in paired settings. We report the average Mean Absolute Error (MAE) under leave-one-system-out (LOSO) protocol to quantify this observation}{figure.2}{}}
