\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces MAE of benchmark score estimators as a function of the number of executed tasks for SWE-bench Verified (top) and Terminal-Bench 2.0 (bottom) under three different realistic evaluation protocols: leave-one-system-out (left), leave-one-family-out (center), and leave-one-harness-out (right). Shaded areas represent $ \pm 1 $ S.E. The \textsc  {trubric}{} and IRT combination dominates (i.e., is never worse and is sometimes better) across all protocols, datasets, and number of executed tasks.}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
